config SCACHE_MEMORY
	tristate "StreamCache two-layer memory management"
	default n
	help
	  Two-layer page pool for high-performance buffered I/O.

	  Layer 1 is a system-level pool with per-CPU regions that
	  pre-allocates pages at init time, bypassing the buddy allocator
	  on the I/O critical path.  Layer 2 is a per-file cache that
	  batches allocations from the pool for near-zero allocation
	  latency.

	  Runtime configuration is via /sys/fs/sc_memory/.

	  If unsure, say N.

config SCACHE_MEMORY_TEST
	tristate "StreamCache memory management self-tests"
	depends on SCACHE_MEMORY
	default n
	help
	  Kernel module that runs self-tests for the StreamCache memory
	  pool at load time and prints results to dmesg.  The module
	  automatically unloads after running.

	  If unsure, say N.
